# The deployed table server. Baked in at build time, so it belongs in the repo
# rather than in whoever's shell happens to run the build — a production bundle
# pointing at localhost is a silent failure, not a loud one.
#
# A subdomain of the site's own domain rather than workers.dev, so the app and
# the API are same-site: a login session belongs in an HttpOnly cookie, and that
# only works cleanly when the two share a registrable domain.
VITE_SERVER_ORIGIN=https://api.ericonice.com

# Where the web app itself is served — distinct from the Worker above, and
# needed so an invite link built inside the Capacitor shell names a real
# address rather than `capacitor://localhost`, which only this device's app
# can open. See `inviteLink` in `serverUrl.ts`.
VITE_APP_ORIGIN=https://honeymoon-bridge.ericonice.com
